From 9da7451d10eac0cf6b5bec5e40c502197987fade Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:31:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-98: a colour typed in and the eyedropper, like
 WPF's brush editor (0.98.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WPF (the Properties window's brush editor): a colour can be typed in (its hex
value) and picked from the screen (the eyedropper). Here Color / Font.Color had
the colour well and BCB6's 16 colours only. Now under the swatches: a text box
(#rrggbb, #rgb or a BCB6 name like clRed / clNavy, Enter; a bad one is marked
and nothing is sent) and 滴管 (window.EyeDropper: a click anywhere on the
screen -- the design surface too -- is the colour; Esc gives up; disabled
where there is no eyedropper). colorText() turns what is typed into #rrggbb.

WPF_DIFF_LOG.md: 0.97 commit filled in; the "Configure XAML Designer" page
added as a source with new open items 28-31 (zoom by using, default zoom,
default document view, the snapline spacing).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 160, smoke 186, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (#abc -> #aabbcc, clRed -> #ff0000, zzz marked and not sent; the
eyedropper (a stand-in answering #123456) -> setLook color #123456).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
